WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:05.308
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.390 --> 00:08.692
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.777 --> 00:12.162
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.230 --> 00:15.149
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:15.200 --> 00:18.736
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.820 --> 00:21.956
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:22.023 --> 00:23.557
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.625 --> 00:24.975
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:25.043 --> 00:29.334
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.137 --> 00:37.054
ANNOUNCER: Need to move?

00:37.138 --> 00:38.055
No problem.

00:38.139 --> 00:39.957
Take it yourself with U-Haul.

00:40.025 --> 00:41.558
But I've never driven
a truck before.

00:41.626 --> 00:42.860
<i>ANNOUNCER: No problem.</i>

00:42.927 --> 00:45.212
<i>U-Haul lets anyone drive
a giant truck,</i>

00:45.280 --> 00:48.649
<i>even though it's dangerous,
because, hey, you're moving.</i>

00:48.716 --> 00:51.652
(horns honking,
tires screeching)

00:51.719 --> 00:55.239
Sorry, I'm making a go
of it in a new city.

00:55.323 --> 00:57.441
All right, I'll see you
guys in a couple of days.

00:57.509 --> 00:58.742
Where are you going?

00:58.810 --> 01:00.311
I'm off to take pictures
of lesbian butts.

01:00.378 --> 01:01.795
What?

01:01.863 --> 01:03.914
Joe and Quagmire and I are
making a coffee table book

01:03.982 --> 01:05.949
<i>called Lesbian Butts
in '80s Jeans.</i>

01:06.017 --> 01:08.319
I already got the first
chapter right here.

01:08.386 --> 01:10.387
Where'd you take
all these pictures?

01:10.455 --> 01:12.539
You know, coffee houses,
Chevy dealerships,

01:12.590 --> 01:13.924
all the usual places.

01:13.992 --> 01:14.925
Peter, you're not
doing that.

01:14.993 --> 01:16.460
I got a ton
of errands to run,

01:16.544 --> 01:18.095
and I need your help
around here.

01:18.163 --> 01:19.730
Well, fine, if I
can't do the book

01:19.798 --> 01:21.265
I'm gonna hurt
something you love.

01:22.701 --> 01:26.270
(grunting)

01:26.354 --> 01:27.554
(coughing)

01:27.605 --> 01:29.039
You happy now?

01:29.107 --> 01:31.158
Maybe we should discuss this
in the other room.

01:31.226 --> 01:32.760
I don't like fighting
in front of the kids.

01:32.827 --> 01:34.561
No, I want to fight
in front of the kids.

01:34.629 --> 01:36.447
I feed off the excitement
of an audience.

01:36.514 --> 01:38.048
Peter, for once
you're going to stay here

01:38.116 --> 01:39.316
and help
around the house.

01:39.384 --> 01:41.418
Now, I need you to watch
Stewie till I get back.

01:43.421 --> 01:45.622
Whoever did this, thank you.

01:50.311 --> 01:51.345
All right, Stewie,
since Lois says

01:51.413 --> 01:52.579
I got to keep
an eye on you,

01:52.647 --> 01:54.848
we might as well have
some father-son time,

01:54.916 --> 01:56.066
so I'm gonna measure
your penis

01:56.134 --> 01:57.735
and then I'm gonna
measure my penis,

01:57.802 --> 01:59.403
and we're gonna see
whose is bigger.

01:59.471 --> 02:00.571
Doesn't really
seem fair.

02:00.638 --> 02:02.523
All right, let's see
what you got.

02:02.590 --> 02:04.975
Stupid game anyway.

02:05.043 --> 02:06.643
ANNOUNCER:
Hey, kids, coming up next,

02:06.711 --> 02:08.946
<i>it's the Jolly Farm Revue
marathon.</i>

02:09.013 --> 02:10.097
No, no, don't
switch it.

02:10.148 --> 02:10.964
<i>I want to watch
Jolly Farm.</i>

02:11.015 --> 02:12.433
Son of a bitch.

02:12.500 --> 02:14.968
I got to spend the rest of the
day watching stupid kid shows.

02:15.036 --> 02:16.653
I'd rather watch paint dry.

02:17.856 --> 02:19.707
(sexy music playing)

02:27.165 --> 02:28.999
Nice.

02:32.537 --> 02:34.238
Wakey, wakey.

02:34.305 --> 02:36.240
ALL:
Good morning, Mother Maggie.

02:36.307 --> 02:37.641
Heh, who's this?

02:37.709 --> 02:38.776
I like this lady.

02:38.843 --> 02:40.077
Hey, do you think
Mother Maggie

02:40.145 --> 02:41.345
is married to
Father Fa...?

02:41.413 --> 02:42.829
Oh, probably not.

02:42.881 --> 02:44.181
MOTHER MAGGIE:
And the unicorn slid

02:44.265 --> 02:47.034
down the rainbow
to a field of jellybeans

02:47.102 --> 02:49.203
where she
and the other villagers decided

02:49.270 --> 02:52.106
it had been the best day ever.

02:52.173 --> 02:54.124
Oh, look, it's Pengrove Pig,

02:54.192 --> 02:56.660
and he's sharing
his apples nicely, isn't he?

02:56.728 --> 02:58.946
Like a champ he is.

02:59.013 --> 03:03.367
♪ Head, shoulders, knees,
and toes, knees and toes. ♪

03:03.435 --> 03:06.804
And that's how you make a duck
out of an oatmeal container.

03:06.871 --> 03:09.807
This is the greatest show
in the history of television.

03:09.874 --> 03:12.776
Mother Maggie, you are
a kindred spirit.

03:12.844 --> 03:14.778
This must be how twins
who are separated at birth

03:14.846 --> 03:16.547
feel when they first meet.

03:21.069 --> 03:22.970
Trade house keys,
bang each other's wives?

03:23.037 --> 03:24.872
Yep.

03:29.611 --> 03:32.179
I can't dissect
this pig, Mr. Kingman.

03:32.247 --> 03:33.647
It's against
my religion.

03:33.715 --> 03:34.948
Believe me, Neil,
it's no thrill

03:35.016 --> 03:36.617
for the pig to
touch a Jew either.

03:36.684 --> 03:38.418
Okay, how about you,
Meg, how are you doing?

03:38.486 --> 03:39.953
Pretty good.

03:40.021 --> 03:42.890
It's, it's kind of cool
cutting something that's not me.

03:42.957 --> 03:44.925
Wow, that's some
very impressive work.

03:44.993 --> 03:47.861
It's easy for Meg to dissect
a pig because she is a pig.

03:47.929 --> 03:48.929
(laughs)

03:48.997 --> 03:50.347
Hey!

03:50.415 --> 03:51.982
All right,
I'll let that one slide.

03:52.050 --> 03:53.717
Meg, you have some
real potential.

03:53.785 --> 03:55.285
Have you ever thought
about becoming a doctor

03:55.353 --> 03:56.487
when you grow up?

03:56.554 --> 03:58.755
I always just assumed
I'd work on the docks.

03:58.823 --> 04:00.157
Don't limit
yourself, Meg.

04:00.225 --> 04:01.925
Doctors wear a mask
most of the time,

04:01.993 --> 04:03.727
so this isn't
an issue.

04:03.795 --> 04:05.512
If you're interested
the school has a program

04:05.580 --> 04:07.080
where you can shadow
a real doctor

04:07.148 --> 04:08.849
and learn more about
the medical field.

04:08.917 --> 04:11.034
Yeah, wow, I'd love
to check that out.

04:11.102 --> 04:12.286
Great, I'll
set it up.

04:12.353 --> 04:13.971
I didn't know a pig
could be a doctor.

04:14.038 --> 04:15.072
Hey!

04:15.139 --> 04:17.140
You get
just a few more of those.

04:20.411 --> 04:22.184
MOTHER MAGGIE:
Now, children, we're going

04:22.209 --> 04:23.696
to learn who wears a hat.

04:23.815 --> 04:25.649
Can a fireman wear
a hat?

04:25.717 --> 04:27.284
KIDS: Yes.
No? Yes.

04:27.352 --> 04:29.253
Can a policeman
wear a hat?

04:29.320 --> 04:30.187
KIDS: Yes.
No way.

04:30.255 --> 04:31.338
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yes.

04:31.406 --> 04:32.739
Yes, he can, I knew that.

04:32.807 --> 04:36.043
Now, you at home, tell me,
who else wears a hat?

04:36.110 --> 04:37.778
A very formal horse?

04:37.846 --> 04:39.279
Very good.

04:39.347 --> 04:43.417
Even a bowling ball can wear a
hat if you use your imagination.

04:43.468 --> 04:46.453
(laughing):
A bowling ball wearing a hat?

04:46.521 --> 04:48.956
This is what high-def
was invented for.

04:49.023 --> 04:51.124
Peter, what the hell
are you doing?

04:51.192 --> 04:52.726
Being a good dad
like you asked.

04:52.794 --> 04:54.294
<i>I've been watching
Jolly Farm with Stewie</i>

04:54.362 --> 04:55.562
for the last
three hours.

04:55.630 --> 04:58.265
That's not Stewie,
that's a pineapple.

04:58.333 --> 05:00.334
Oh, my God, where is Stewie?

05:00.401 --> 05:01.602
I don't know, but
I'm sure he's fine.

05:01.669 --> 05:02.603
Peter, he's a baby.

05:02.670 --> 05:04.238
You can't leave him alone.

05:04.305 --> 05:06.156
Come on, it's good to
have some alone time.

05:06.224 --> 05:08.392
You know, I spent a year
alone on a desert island

05:08.459 --> 05:10.360
with nothing but a monkey
to keep me company.

05:10.428 --> 05:12.963
You're saved, sir, we're going
to get you back to civilization.

05:13.031 --> 05:14.765
And how about we bring along
your monkey pal?

05:14.832 --> 05:15.983
Okay.

05:16.050 --> 05:17.434
Yeah, we can teach
him sign language

05:17.502 --> 05:18.802
and he can
tell us stories

05:18.870 --> 05:20.637
about what you two did
on the island together.

05:20.705 --> 05:23.257
No, n-no, no, no, let's, let's
not, let's not bring the monkey.

05:23.324 --> 05:25.792
Um, I have a peanut M&M
up my nose

05:25.860 --> 05:28.562
and it's now further up
than my finger can reach.

05:28.630 --> 05:30.664
I am ready to farm
this out to someone.

05:30.732 --> 05:32.633
Oh, Stewie, there you are.

05:32.684 --> 05:35.385
Peter, I asked you to do one
simple thing-- watch the baby--

05:35.453 --> 05:36.987
and you couldn't even do that.

05:37.055 --> 05:38.555
Come on, Stewie.

05:38.640 --> 05:40.557
Geez, why's she got
to be such a nag?

05:40.642 --> 05:42.559
I wish she was more
like Mother Maggie.

05:42.627 --> 05:45.529
Mother Maggie has an
announcement, lads and lasses.

05:45.597 --> 05:47.965
I've had such fun playing
and learning with you

05:48.032 --> 05:50.734
these last few years, but now,

05:50.802 --> 05:55.038
just as bees must leave the
hive, I must leave Jolly Farm--

05:55.106 --> 05:57.608
not that you asked, but to have
fertility treatments--

05:57.675 --> 06:01.311
<i>so this will be our last episode
of Jolly Farm.</i>

06:01.379 --> 06:02.579
What? No.

06:02.647 --> 06:04.481
<i>They can't cancel Jolly Farm.</i>

06:04.549 --> 06:06.199
Peter, it's just a
stupid kids' show.

06:06.267 --> 06:08.001
Just a stupid
kids' show?

06:08.052 --> 06:10.637
What about Pengrove Pig
and the Lollipop Luau?

06:10.705 --> 06:12.072
I-I-I don't know.

06:12.140 --> 06:13.407
This is going
to leave a void,

06:13.474 --> 06:15.058
and somebody's got
to fill it.

06:15.126 --> 06:16.193
I think you're
overreacting.

06:16.260 --> 06:17.594
You don't understand,
Brian.

06:17.662 --> 06:19.646
<i>What am I supposed to do
without Jolly Farm?</i>

06:19.714 --> 06:22.582
I'll be like an Italian mom
without bad kids.

06:22.650 --> 06:26.219
Hey, hey, hey, what the hell
is all the commotion in here?

06:26.270 --> 06:27.371
We're not doing anything.

06:27.438 --> 06:28.805
You getting
fresh with me?

06:28.873 --> 06:30.874
I'm tired of bailing both
of youse out of prison.

06:30.942 --> 06:32.075
We're both
in college

06:32.143 --> 06:33.710
and we consistently make
the dean's list.

06:33.778 --> 06:35.012
I'm telling
your father.

06:35.079 --> 06:36.113
Good.

06:39.651 --> 06:41.685
Where the hell
is our food?

06:41.753 --> 06:43.186
Yeah, where are
Mom and Dad?

06:43.254 --> 06:44.888
And where's
that awesome finger painting

06:44.956 --> 06:45.856
Stewie did this morning?

06:45.923 --> 06:46.890
Oh, here it is.

06:46.958 --> 06:47.991
Thank you for bringing it up.

06:48.059 --> 06:49.359
I wasn't going to bring it up.

06:49.427 --> 06:51.128
Well, what's
going on?

06:51.195 --> 06:52.029
You haven't
eaten yet?

06:52.096 --> 06:53.030
No.

06:53.097 --> 06:54.331
Where's your father?

06:54.399 --> 06:56.199
He was supposed to put
the lasagna in the oven.

06:56.267 --> 06:58.902
I ask him to do one thing
while I'm at yoga.

06:58.970 --> 07:00.604
You go to an intro class

07:00.672 --> 07:02.172
and it's not even
at the yoga studio.

07:02.240 --> 07:03.390
It's in someone's living room.

07:03.458 --> 07:04.925
And that's not even a yoga mat.

07:04.993 --> 07:07.094
That's the old pee pad
from my crib.

07:07.161 --> 07:09.696
Uh, Lois, you might want
to check this out.

07:09.764 --> 07:12.315
What is it, Brian?
Take a look.

07:12.400 --> 07:17.237
<i>PETER: And now, boys and girls,
it's time for Petey's Funhouse.</i>

07:17.288 --> 07:20.407
(children cheering)

07:20.475 --> 07:23.410
♪ It's gonna be fun
and we'll have lots of yuks ♪

07:23.461 --> 07:25.979
♪ And maybe learn some stuff
but not definitely ♪

07:26.047 --> 07:29.299
<i>♪ It's the Petey's Funhouse
show. ♪</i>

07:29.367 --> 07:31.935
Ugh, another
Aaron Sorkin show

07:32.003 --> 07:33.937
that's way over
everyone's head.

07:39.852 --> 07:42.687
How the hell did you even get
a TV show, Peter?

07:42.755 --> 07:44.355
I just answered an
ad off Craigslist,

07:44.423 --> 07:47.291
and after several hours of
sexual torture, I had a show.

07:47.359 --> 07:48.292
(phone rings)

07:48.360 --> 07:49.427
Don't answer that.

07:49.495 --> 07:51.095
I gave out that
number under duress.

07:51.163 --> 07:53.397
Lois, Peter's show is on the
local public access channel.

07:53.465 --> 07:54.899
Anyone can have one.

07:54.967 --> 07:56.701
<i>Yeah, Petey's Funhouse
is actually replacing</i>

07:56.769 --> 07:58.903
<i>The Bad Audio Basement Show.</i>

07:58.971 --> 08:02.540
(distorted): And once the hot glue dries,
your birdhouse will be complete.

08:02.608 --> 08:04.575
Peter, you already do
nothing around the house

08:04.643 --> 08:07.011
and now you're wasting
more time with this nonsense.

08:07.078 --> 08:09.280
Geez, you're still getting
on my hump about this?

08:09.348 --> 08:10.481
I help out
around here.

08:10.549 --> 08:12.216
Just this morning I
changed Meg's diaper

08:12.284 --> 08:13.651
and I sent her
off to school.

08:13.719 --> 08:16.220
Boy, can she kick, but
she left here spotless.

08:20.409 --> 08:22.510
Dr. Hartman, thanks for
letting me shadow you.

08:22.578 --> 08:24.679
I just know I'm going
to learn so much.

08:24.746 --> 08:27.048
It's my pleasure, Meg,
and you're in good hands.

08:27.115 --> 08:28.449
You see that diploma?

08:28.517 --> 08:29.951
Yale Medical School.

08:30.018 --> 08:31.819
Wow, that's
impressive.

08:31.887 --> 08:34.388
Thank you, I work very hard
on my calligraphy.

08:34.456 --> 08:36.991
So, how about we take a little
stroll around the hospital?

08:37.075 --> 08:39.109
This area is known
as a hallway.

08:39.161 --> 08:40.461
Don't worry,
you'll pick up

08:40.546 --> 08:42.947
on all the technical
doctor jargon pretty soon.

08:42.998 --> 08:45.883
Hey, is it prescription
or perscription?

08:45.951 --> 08:47.335
I think
it's prescription.

08:47.419 --> 08:50.338
Prescription... that just
feels weird in my mouth.

08:50.422 --> 08:53.057
Perscription is better.

08:53.124 --> 08:54.625
Oh, and there's the E.R.

08:54.676 --> 08:57.178
Don't go in there unless you
want everyone to yell at you.

09:03.502 --> 09:06.137
Hi, kids, I'm Petey Griffin.

09:06.205 --> 09:07.738
ALL: Hi, Petey!

09:07.806 --> 09:10.324
<i>We're going to have so much fun
on Petey's Funhouse today,</i>

09:10.392 --> 09:14.262
but before we begin, your friend
Petey wants to sing you a song.

09:15.564 --> 09:18.015
♪ What makes you
so special? ♪

09:18.083 --> 09:20.801
♪ The fact
that you are special ♪

09:20.869 --> 09:23.154
♪ But if everybody's
special ♪

09:23.222 --> 09:25.873
♪ That kinda
waters it down ♪

09:25.941 --> 09:28.526
♪ So some of you
ain't special ♪

09:28.594 --> 09:31.279
♪ I can tell you
who is special ♪

09:31.346 --> 09:33.497
♪ Like you and you
ain't special. ♪

09:33.565 --> 09:35.299
And you are
and you're not.

09:37.436 --> 09:41.305
<i>Okay, kids, it's story time here
on Petey's Funhouse.</i>

09:41.373 --> 09:44.809
<i>Today's story is
Lesbian Butts in '80s Jeans.</i>

09:44.877 --> 09:46.844
Ooh, that's a classic.

09:46.912 --> 09:50.448
Once upon a time, some chick in
a leather jacket in front of me

09:50.515 --> 09:52.750
in the parking lot walked
into Home Depot,

09:52.818 --> 09:55.453
and her butt looked like this.

09:55.520 --> 09:57.054
Everybody see this?

09:57.122 --> 09:59.323
Everybody see
how shapeless this is?

09:59.391 --> 10:02.827
She walked out of there with
a bag of soil on each shoulder.

10:02.895 --> 10:04.495
Now, before I show you
this next one,

10:04.563 --> 10:07.882
has anyone here ever heard
of the Sturgis Motorcycle Rally?

10:10.085 --> 10:12.653
<i>I know we have a lot of yuks
here on Petey's Funhouse,</i>

10:12.721 --> 10:15.323
but one thing
that's not fun is a bully.

10:15.390 --> 10:17.925
Now, how many of you kids out
there have ever gotten bullied?

10:19.027 --> 10:20.161
Aw, come on up here

10:20.228 --> 10:22.330
and tell us
about it, champ.

10:22.397 --> 10:27.301
Well, my name is Winston,
and I'm quite fond of ballet.

10:27.369 --> 10:29.470
One time I tried out
for Little League

10:29.538 --> 10:31.973
in my ballet shoes,
and the other kids made

10:32.040 --> 10:34.442
so much fun of me,
I wet my pants.

10:34.509 --> 10:36.077
What, wait,
what, like pee?

10:36.144 --> 10:37.545
How old were you?
Eight.

10:37.613 --> 10:38.779
Aah, too old!

10:38.847 --> 10:41.115
Too old to be peeing yourself,
Baby Pee Pants.

10:41.183 --> 10:42.917
All right,
you kids finish him off.

10:47.623 --> 10:48.756
Hey, what do you
got there?

10:48.824 --> 10:50.391
Oh, I'm just playing
with some Lee Logs.

10:50.459 --> 10:51.859
What the hell
are Lee Logs?

10:51.927 --> 10:53.527
A little something I
created-- Lee Logs.

10:53.595 --> 10:54.895
Robert E. Lee.

10:54.963 --> 10:56.831
You know, you got Lincoln
Logs, you got Lee Logs.

10:56.898 --> 10:58.766
I don't get it, can,
can you build a house?

10:58.834 --> 11:00.101
You can build
quarters.

11:00.168 --> 11:01.569
And people live there?

11:01.637 --> 11:03.571
They live there if you
tell 'em to live there.

11:03.639 --> 11:05.473
I don't know if I like
the idea of Lee Logs.

11:05.540 --> 11:07.141
Yeah, they're not
selling very well.

11:07.209 --> 11:08.909
Peter, dinner!

11:08.977 --> 11:10.161
No dinner for
me tonight, Lois.

11:10.228 --> 11:12.430
I have to go work on
a bit for tomorrow's show.

11:12.497 --> 11:14.665
If I can kill 25
butterflies in a minute,

11:14.733 --> 11:16.767
I won't have to show
the audience my balls.

11:16.835 --> 11:18.869
Peter, this is the
fourth night in a row

11:18.937 --> 11:21.038
you've skipped out on us
to work on your show.

11:21.106 --> 11:23.274
Once again, I'm gonna be stuck
cleaning up the kitchen,

11:23.342 --> 11:25.810
helping out with homework,
and bathing Stewie.

11:25.877 --> 11:27.678
You know, I'd lay off
the nagging if I was you.

11:27.746 --> 11:29.046
I'm a children's TV star now.

11:29.114 --> 11:30.815
I can have any three-year-old
girl I want.

11:30.882 --> 11:32.383
Just know that, Lois.

11:32.451 --> 11:34.518
Peter, I'm only asking
you to do your share.

11:34.586 --> 11:35.686
Well, it's getting
on my nerves.

11:35.754 --> 11:36.821
Like, right now,

11:36.888 --> 11:38.089
you are the most
annoying thing

11:38.156 --> 11:40.691
in my life, with the
possible exception of Evite.

11:40.759 --> 11:42.560
What's this?
It's this Web site you can use

11:42.627 --> 11:43.828
to invite people
to stuff.

11:43.895 --> 11:45.813
Does it have to be
a significant event?

11:45.881 --> 11:47.298
No. Not at all!

11:47.366 --> 11:48.766
Well, do you just
get the invitation,

11:48.834 --> 11:50.167
and that's the end of it?

11:50.235 --> 11:52.119
No, it'll remind you
about it constantly!

11:52.187 --> 11:54.522
Is there any way
I can customize this

11:54.589 --> 11:57.358
to showcase my personality
through familiar clip art?

11:57.426 --> 11:58.726
Yes!

11:58.794 --> 12:00.277
And what about
those replying?

12:00.345 --> 12:02.163
Can they demonstrate
their sense of humor

12:02.230 --> 12:03.564
through hilarious replies?

12:03.632 --> 12:06.033
Yes, yes, yes to
everything you're saying!

12:06.101 --> 12:08.469
I'm so excited
to get started!

12:08.537 --> 12:10.705
You do that while
I jump out this window!

12:10.772 --> 12:12.506
(glass shatters)

12:12.574 --> 12:15.376
<i>ANNOUNCER: Evite. Tell a friend
and then kill yourself.</i>

12:18.780 --> 12:20.314
And then when you
get a little older,

12:20.382 --> 12:21.949
stuff will come out.

12:22.017 --> 12:23.751
(old-timey car horn honks)

12:23.819 --> 12:25.219
Uh-oh!

12:25.287 --> 12:28.072
Sounds like my cranky
new neighbor just got home.

12:28.140 --> 12:29.740
I hope she doesn't
come over here

12:29.808 --> 12:31.175
and give me the business.

12:31.243 --> 12:32.293
(knocking)

12:32.360 --> 12:33.477
Peter!

12:33.545 --> 12:35.746
Oh, hi, Saggy Naggy.

12:35.814 --> 12:37.431
Never mind with "hi!"

12:37.499 --> 12:40.634
It sounds like someone's
having fun over here!

12:40.702 --> 12:42.670
You know I don't
like that!

12:42.738 --> 12:45.005
Hey, kids.
Meet Saggy Naggy.

12:45.073 --> 12:47.141
Real nice lady, huh?

12:47.209 --> 12:48.709
AUDIENCE: No!

12:48.777 --> 12:50.344
What can I do for you,
Saggy Naggy?

12:50.412 --> 12:52.029
You can stop having fun!

12:52.097 --> 12:54.782
But we like fun,
don't we, kids?

12:54.850 --> 12:56.067
AUDIENCE: Yes!

12:56.134 --> 12:57.401
Well, too bad,

12:57.469 --> 12:58.936
'cause you're all gonna
eat your vegetables,

12:59.004 --> 13:01.222
listen to long stories
about my cousins,

13:01.289 --> 13:03.441
and help me
fold sheets!

13:03.508 --> 13:05.676
And you! You're gonna
help around the house,

13:05.744 --> 13:06.844
take out the garbage,

13:06.895 --> 13:08.996
and give Stewie
his bottle!

13:09.064 --> 13:10.731
Yeah, I heard it.
They say my name

13:10.799 --> 13:12.967
on TV all the time;
calm down, bitch.

13:13.034 --> 13:14.802
<i>Make me dinner,
and go rent Twilight,</i>

13:14.870 --> 13:16.687
and do mouth
stuff on me,

13:16.755 --> 13:19.056
even though it's been a
day-and-a-half since I've showered,

13:19.124 --> 13:21.792
and I've used several public
bathrooms in the interim!

13:21.860 --> 13:24.228
Sounds like this could
go on for a while, kids.

13:24.296 --> 13:25.379
Hey, Saggy Naggy,

13:25.447 --> 13:27.281
I know what'll cheer you up.

13:27.349 --> 13:28.649
Do you like pie?

13:28.717 --> 13:30.067
I guess.

13:30.118 --> 13:31.986
Well, how does this taste?

13:32.053 --> 13:35.039
(audience cheers)

13:35.107 --> 13:36.490
Well, I guess she thought

13:36.558 --> 13:38.793
it was a no-pies-in-the-face
kind of neighborhood.

13:38.860 --> 13:42.496
Wrong assessment
of the neighborhood, sweetheart!

13:46.201 --> 13:47.701
And how are you today, Mr...

13:47.769 --> 13:48.936
Pa-ti-ent?

13:49.004 --> 13:50.538
My last name is Saunders.

13:50.605 --> 13:52.523
That's an interesting
pronunciation.

13:52.591 --> 13:54.291
This is Meg; she's
shadowing me today.

13:54.359 --> 13:56.427
And boy, could she put
the applesauce away

13:56.495 --> 13:58.312
in the commissary.
Hi.

13:58.396 --> 14:00.264
Little tip, Meg:
The inside of this folder

14:00.332 --> 14:02.166
has a diagram
of the human body.

14:02.234 --> 14:03.501
Kind of a cheat sheet.

14:05.053 --> 14:07.488
Now see, right now,
I'm listening for cancer.

14:07.556 --> 14:09.773
Do you mean
his heartbeat?

14:09.841 --> 14:11.826
Maybe. Here,
you take a turn.

14:13.245 --> 14:15.446
Wow, your heartbeat
sounds a little fast.

14:15.514 --> 14:17.681
Do you smoke?
Actually, I do.

14:17.749 --> 14:19.483
Ah, me, too.
Isn't it great?

14:19.551 --> 14:20.885
Well, that's
bad for you.

14:20.952 --> 14:21.986
You shouldn't do it.

14:22.053 --> 14:23.320
It raises your heart rate

14:23.388 --> 14:25.156
and can lead
to emphysema or cancer.

14:25.223 --> 14:27.107
That's impressive, Meg.
It's no big deal.

14:27.175 --> 14:29.109
It's just stuff
I learned in health class.

14:29.177 --> 14:30.811
Well, you're clearly
a bright, young lady.

14:30.879 --> 14:32.513
And you've got quite a...

14:32.581 --> 14:34.565
head on your...

14:34.633 --> 14:35.766
shoulders.

14:35.834 --> 14:37.067
Thanks.

14:37.135 --> 14:39.503
Dr. Hartman, you just got
this urgent message.

14:39.571 --> 14:40.988
Oh, dear.
Prilosec, huh?

14:41.056 --> 14:42.256
No, it's below that.

14:42.324 --> 14:43.490
Oh.

14:43.558 --> 14:44.625
Oh, my God.

14:44.693 --> 14:45.843
Meg, I'm afraid
my brother

14:45.911 --> 14:47.211
just tried to kill
himself in prison.

14:47.279 --> 14:48.746
I-I have to go.

14:48.813 --> 14:50.781
You're gonna have to take
things from here, I guess.

14:50.849 --> 14:52.183
What?! What are you
talking about?

14:52.250 --> 14:54.401
Well, you now know
about as much as I do

14:54.469 --> 14:55.652
about this whole
doctor thing.

14:55.704 --> 14:57.204
But I have no formal
medical training.

14:57.272 --> 14:59.273
Ah, you'll be fine.
I think that book on the shelf

14:59.341 --> 15:01.008
has most of the
stuff in there.

15:01.076 --> 15:03.677
And don't forget the cheat sheet
if you need a helping...

15:03.745 --> 15:05.663
hand.

15:10.235 --> 15:11.402
Are we really
buying fish

15:11.469 --> 15:13.804
at the same place
we buy tires?

15:13.872 --> 15:16.106
And, w-what... "Fazio"?

15:16.174 --> 15:18.509
What, is that a brand
of Blu-ray player?

15:18.577 --> 15:20.928
Stewie, this sweatshirt
is so sophisticated.

15:20.996 --> 15:22.997
Look, it says New York.

15:23.064 --> 15:24.965
People will think
I'm from there.

15:25.033 --> 15:26.200
(children laughing)

15:27.719 --> 15:30.354
Put your phone away;
we're at a funeral!

15:30.422 --> 15:31.956
Oh, my God.

15:32.023 --> 15:33.390
(laughs)
Look!

15:33.458 --> 15:35.125
It's Saggy Naggy.

15:35.193 --> 15:36.110
GROUP:
Boo!

15:36.177 --> 15:37.311
You're mean.

15:37.379 --> 15:38.846
I don't like you,
Saggy Naggy.

15:38.914 --> 15:40.831
You stink, Saggy Naggy.

15:40.899 --> 15:42.566
My goodness, that's
a very rude thing

15:42.634 --> 15:43.801
to say to someone.

15:43.868 --> 15:45.369
Calling them Saggy...

15:45.437 --> 15:46.754
(all laugh)

15:46.821 --> 15:48.155
What the hell?!

15:48.223 --> 15:50.140
Young man, what do
you think you're...

16:03.458 --> 16:05.659
Lois, I just saw
Jessica Alba on television.

16:05.743 --> 16:07.077
We've got 90 seconds;
let's go!

16:07.128 --> 16:08.278
Peter, I'm not
in the mood!

16:08.329 --> 16:09.780
That's okay. We can
do it anyway.

16:09.847 --> 16:12.049
Peter, I was assaulted
in public because of you!

16:12.116 --> 16:13.800
Oh, my God, what happened?!

16:13.868 --> 16:14.968
I'll tell you
what happened.

16:15.036 --> 16:17.137
A group of kids
attacked me at Costmart

16:17.222 --> 16:19.072
because you portrayed
me on your show

16:19.140 --> 16:20.807
as a raging
puppet bitch!

16:20.875 --> 16:22.175
Writers take
from their lives.

16:22.243 --> 16:24.378
You married a creative type.
You knew this was a risk.

16:24.445 --> 16:26.079
What's that
supposed to mean?

16:26.147 --> 16:28.649
Well, the last few weeks, you've
been nagging the hell out of me.

16:28.716 --> 16:30.250
Peter, you think
I like nagging you?

16:30.318 --> 16:32.552
One of us needs to be
an adult in this marriage,

16:32.620 --> 16:33.987
and it's clearly not you.

16:34.055 --> 16:36.290
Is this about me wetting
the bed just now?

16:36.357 --> 16:37.591
Peter, don't
you understand

16:37.659 --> 16:39.526
that I'm just looking
out for this family?

16:39.594 --> 16:40.694
Besides, without
my nagging,

16:40.762 --> 16:42.629
you'd probably
get yourself killed.

16:42.697 --> 16:45.232
Or laid. Right,
frat house?

16:45.300 --> 16:47.634
Yeah!
(cheering and whooping)

16:47.702 --> 16:50.537
(laughs) Those knuckleheads
should be studying.

16:50.605 --> 16:52.572
Okay, you know what?
Fine, Peter, that's it.

16:52.640 --> 16:54.241
From now on, I'm not
nagging you anymore.

16:54.309 --> 16:55.309
You're not?

16:55.376 --> 16:57.010
No, you're on your own.

16:57.078 --> 16:59.730
I'm done with it.
I'm done with all of it!

16:59.797 --> 17:02.165
Well, great, I should
probably get some sleep.

17:02.233 --> 17:04.368
Tomorrow on Petey's Funhouse,
we're doing who's on first.

17:04.435 --> 17:05.669
I'm gonna play
Costello,

17:05.737 --> 17:08.305
and Abbott is gonna
be played by live puma.

17:08.373 --> 17:10.907
Peter, that sounds
really d...

17:10.975 --> 17:12.743
you know what?
Sounds great.

17:12.810 --> 17:14.011
Have fun.

17:14.078 --> 17:16.797
Thanks, Lois.
Good night.

17:16.864 --> 17:19.933
Lois? Other families
fight, too, right?

17:20.001 --> 17:21.535
Not this much.

17:21.602 --> 17:23.270
Do you think maybe
we should think about

17:23.338 --> 17:24.805
getting a...
It is what it is.

17:24.872 --> 17:26.840
Let's just get Stewie to
college and go from there.

17:30.078 --> 17:31.712
Sir, if you're gonna
want me to examine

17:31.779 --> 17:33.146
where you're
having an issue,

17:33.214 --> 17:35.615
you're gonna have to be more
specific than "thingee".

17:35.683 --> 17:38.018
Okay. It's not
the front thingee.

17:38.086 --> 17:39.803
What's going on in here?

17:39.871 --> 17:41.305
Where's Dr. Hartman?

17:41.372 --> 17:43.840
He had a family emergency.
I'm not really a doctor

17:43.908 --> 17:45.642
but I've been sort of
filling in for him.

17:45.710 --> 17:46.910
You what?!

17:46.978 --> 17:49.313
Well, I think I want
to go into medicine,

17:49.380 --> 17:50.814
so I was shadowing
Dr. Hartman.

17:50.881 --> 17:52.516
I've actually
been learning a lot,

17:52.583 --> 17:54.318
but then he just left me here!

17:54.385 --> 17:55.752
Well, you don't belong here!

17:55.820 --> 17:57.854
This is a professional
medical institution

17:57.922 --> 18:00.123
with standards
and regulations to adhere to!

18:00.191 --> 18:01.191
But, but I...

18:01.259 --> 18:02.993
I'm gonna have to
ask you to leave.

18:03.061 --> 18:05.128
I'm sorry.
I'll go.

18:07.298 --> 18:08.632
(bottle clinks)

18:10.234 --> 18:12.602
My issue has
resolved itself.

18:16.074 --> 18:17.641
PETER:
And don't go anywhere, kids,

18:17.709 --> 18:19.676
'cause coming up,
we got some classic comedy

18:19.744 --> 18:21.278
with me and a puma.

18:21.346 --> 18:23.213
Is Dad really gonna do this?

18:23.281 --> 18:25.349
I told your father I was
gonna leave him alone.

18:25.416 --> 18:27.517
Saggy Naggy is
keeping out of this.

18:27.585 --> 18:28.919
Is the puma ready?

18:28.986 --> 18:30.587
Maybe we should
poke him with the

18:30.655 --> 18:33.156
"is-the-Puma-ready?"
stick.

18:33.224 --> 18:36.009
(roars loudly)

18:36.077 --> 18:38.145
Oh, my god, I can't
let him do this!

18:38.212 --> 18:40.747
Come on, kids! We got to get
down to that TV studio!

18:40.815 --> 18:42.399
Okay, yeah, just step
on the coloring book.

18:42.450 --> 18:43.333
That's cool.

18:44.635 --> 18:45.802
(brakes screech)

18:48.873 --> 18:51.074
I'm asking you
who's on first?

18:51.125 --> 18:53.744
(screaming)

18:53.795 --> 18:54.778
(audience screams)

18:54.846 --> 18:56.530
Oh, my God! Peter!

18:56.597 --> 18:57.881
Cut the camera! Cut it!

18:57.948 --> 18:59.883
Roll a
"Petey Learn-A-Long Song"!

18:59.950 --> 19:00.917
(screams)

19:00.968 --> 19:02.386
(screams continue)

19:02.453 --> 19:03.737
(to tune
of "The Farmer in the Dell")

19:03.805 --> 19:05.405
PETER: ♪ Kentucky is a state ♪

19:05.473 --> 19:07.707
♪ Kentucky is a state ♪

19:07.775 --> 19:09.976
♪ All the people there
are dicks ♪

19:10.044 --> 19:12.879
♪ Kentucky is a state. ♪

19:12.947 --> 19:14.698
Oh, he's hurt bad.
Someone call 911!

19:14.766 --> 19:15.899
He's bleeding too much!

19:15.966 --> 19:17.434
He needs attention now!

19:17.502 --> 19:19.770
Somebody help him!
Do something!

19:19.837 --> 19:21.671
Now she's nagging everyone.

19:21.739 --> 19:23.507
Does anyone have
any medical training?!

19:23.574 --> 19:25.375
It looks like his
jugular is severed.

19:25.443 --> 19:27.144
I learned this
at the hospital.

19:27.211 --> 19:29.346
Mr. Swanson, find me
a first-aid kit!

19:29.414 --> 19:31.281
Mom, hand me those towels.

19:31.332 --> 19:34.351
Did I hold on to the ball?

19:34.419 --> 19:35.419
Hang in there, Dad.

19:35.486 --> 19:36.853
I'm gonna get you fixed up.

19:45.713 --> 19:46.980
You can do it, Meg.

19:47.048 --> 19:49.666
Come on, Meg.
You've got to save him!

19:49.717 --> 19:52.719
(quietly):
Peter, you need to let go.

20:04.182 --> 20:06.383
L-Lois?

20:06.451 --> 20:07.751
Oh, Peter, thank God!

20:07.819 --> 20:09.085
You're okay.

20:09.153 --> 20:11.421
I guess you were right
about that puma.

20:11.489 --> 20:13.056
I don't know what
I was thinking.

20:13.124 --> 20:14.558
I should've
listened to you.

20:14.625 --> 20:16.560
Peter, I don't
care about that.

20:16.627 --> 20:19.279
I acted like a real jerk,
and I'm sorry, Lois.

20:19.347 --> 20:21.148
I know you just
get on my case

20:21.215 --> 20:22.649
'cause you're
looking out for me.

20:22.717 --> 20:23.884
I am, Peter.

20:23.951 --> 20:25.585
And it's only because
I love you

20:25.653 --> 20:27.988
and I want the best for you
and our family.

20:28.055 --> 20:29.723
I love you, too, Lois.

20:32.160 --> 20:33.827
Isn't anybody
gonna thank me?

20:33.895 --> 20:36.129
Yeah, I'll have a water
if you're getting one.

20:36.197 --> 20:38.415
Mr. Griffin,
you have a visitor.

20:38.483 --> 20:39.633
Hey.

20:39.700 --> 20:41.134
Hey. I get it now.

20:41.202 --> 20:42.969
<i>"Who" is the man's name.</i>

20:43.037 --> 20:45.372
Aha, ah!

20:45.373 --> 21:46.373
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru